To find the membership values, I checked the graph to see which ranges the dirtiness levels fall into and calculated them using linear interpolation
(x-x1) / (x2-x1) for rising slopes and (x2-x) / (x2-x1) for falling slopes. Any terms outside these ranges I evaluated to 0.0.

Person A (Dirtiness = 3.5)
Low:(3.5) = 0.0
Medium:(3.5) = (4.5-3.5) / (4.5-3.0) = 1.0 / 1.5 = 0.67
Large:(3.5) = (3.5-2.5) / (5.0-2.5) = 1.0 / 2.5 = 0.40
Very Large:(3.5) = 0.0

